     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Status of Implementation Progress: Training on APU operations will be provided to 120 loco masters, supervisors and officials of Bangladesh Railway in 10 batches). Already first batch training (12 participants) has started in Ishwardi Upazila from 22 October.

Recommendations for further energy efficiency improvement of rolling stock operations will be made after the project completion.

Training program has been prepared by the consultants. Training will be provided to 120 loco masters, supervisors and officials of Bangladesh Railway in 10 batches.

31 nos. locomotives commissioned.

From Lot 1: 75 nos. luggage vans commissioned, from Lot2: 22 nos. luggage vans waiting to be commissioned.

50 MG Wagon to arrive in Bangladesh by Mid November.

BG wagons are being scheduled to receive in 2024, starting from January.</narrative>
